                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d0f6d5eb-4f1e-40e5-89c7-a62b26ab20c4",
                        "entry_id": "8e0ce767-6cd3-387a-b339-e746af30b2b6",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most slyly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
                        "entry_id": "8e0ce767-6cd3-387a-b339-e746af30b2b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a sly manner, cunningly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd2ef622-88f5-4202-b97c-5c7621ffdf40",
                                "sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
                                "text": "VVhen ſhe vvas dreſt, therefore, dovvn ſhe vvent, reſolved to encounter all the Horrours of the Day, and a moſt diſagreeable one it proved; for Lady Bellaſton took every opportunity very civilly and slily to inſult her; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbdc01ef-0937-486d-af7e-a3aff447452d",
                                "sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
                                "text": "So when they were working that evening at the pumps, there was on this head no small gamesomeness slily going on among them, as they stood with their feet continually overflowed by the rippling clear water; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bff4c4b-64d6-492d-bb68-eb8d6e7275d2",
                                "sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
                                "text": "I lie there on the stretcher-bed and laugh slily, but say nothing; give vent to no opinion one way or the other."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16559656-6952-4164-b6a5-4f361ed57d26",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e0ce767-6cd3-387a-b339-e746af30b2b6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
                        "source_sense_description": "in a sly manner",
                        "target_lang_word": "sournoisement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sournoisement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1af19c7d-cff0-3f63-afdf-0ba0a823c846",
                                        "entry_id": "c62cf84c-3e41-3647-bfdc-8a464f363dda",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’une manière sournoise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd276f96-3e73-4f60-9110-a394c2c4f647",
                                                "sense_id": "1af19c7d-cff0-3f63-afdf-0ba0a823c846",
                                                "text": "Le cabinet de Vienne se déterminait sournoisement à la guerre,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a50a25ef-bedd-411c-8756-493b01efabf9",
                                                "sense_id": "1af19c7d-cff0-3f63-afdf-0ba0a823c846",
                                                "text": "Il pressentait que l’eau triompherait des semelles sans résistance, et, sournoisement, s’infiltrerait jusqu'aux chevilles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66fe3a70-7820-4436-89b5-e4c32c2adb76",
                                                "sense_id": "1af19c7d-cff0-3f63-afdf-0ba0a823c846",
                                                "text": "On n'échappe pas aux morsures de l’ypérite qui, sournoisement, s’accroche à la peau."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71fb032d-085a-428a-b76b-08954977115b",
                                                "sense_id": "1af19c7d-cff0-3f63-afdf-0ba0a823c846",
                                                "text": "Parti de Marrakech pour se rendre à Fez, il ne parvint que jusqu’à l’Oued El-Abid, au Tedla, où il succomba subitement à une maladie qui le minait sournoisement depuis longtemps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99b3ad03-bb12-40a1-b159-3f35bafe6294",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e0ce767-6cd3-387a-b339-e746af30b2b6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ebeda49b-135a-3940-ac20-0cdb11e7050f",
